export anchor ManilaFoldersStyle:
    number: 116
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Manila folders
    idea: The dashboard is a desk file pulled from a steel drawer, with manila folders behind typed tab labels, rubber stamped dates and statuses, and paper clipped cards for the numbers.
    base: light
    palette:
        floor: #e6e3dc, the page behind everything
        drawerSteel: #c8ccc6, the header drawer front
        manila: #ead39b, the main folder and the current tab
        manilaDeep: #dfc282, project folders and back tabs
        folderEdge: #cfae68, edges and stacked sheets, decorative only
        labelWhite: #fbfaf4, typed labels, clipped cards and memos
        ink: #2a2015, text and the primary button
        brown: #59432a, captions and field keys
        stampRed: #a3201a, overdue, Behind and the current tab mark
        stampBlue: #1d3c86, the date stamp, At risk, this week bars and focus
        stampGreen: #2a5a22, the On track stamp
    type:
        Three stacks. Typed is Courier New, Courier, Nimbus Mono PS,
        Liberation Mono, monospace, for labels, figures and keys, often in
        caps with 0.06 to 0.14em tracking. Stamp is Impact, Haettenschweiler,
        Arial Narrow Bold, sans-serif in caps. Body is Gill Sans, Gill Sans
        MT, Trebuchet MS, system-ui, sans-serif. Sizes are 30px bold typed
        greeting, 34 to 40px bold typed figures, 17 to 22px stamps, 13px
        typed caps labels, 14 to 15px sans body and 12px typed caps keys.
    layout:
        A steel drawer front heads the page with a brass label holder
        showing the brand, a drawer pull, and the search, a black New
        project button, the bell and the user in typed caps. Below it the
        navigation is a row of manila folder tabs with typed white labels,
        the current tab taller and joined to the main folder. The main
        folder has two offset deeper manila sheets behind it like a stack.
        Inside, the typed greeting and a red rubber stamp reading 4 tasks
        overdue sit left, and a round blue Received stamp with 31 OCT 2026
        sits right. Four white cards held by steel paper clips carry the
        figures, each turned slightly. Six project folders follow in three
        columns, each with its own tab at a staggered position holding the
        typed name, a key and value list for team, tasks and due date, a big
        typed percent, a striped tally bar and a tilted status stamp. At the
        bottom a clipped memo holds the chart as two typed horizontal bar
        lists, last week in ink and this week in blue with totals, and a
        routing slip lists activity with boxed initials. Folders go two
        across below 980px and one across below 640px.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 48px between folder rows to leave room for tabs, 28 to 32px folder padding.
    density: Medium. One project per folder, facts as a short key and value list.
    corners: Folder tabs 8 to 10px on top, folders 4 to 6px except the corner under the tab, labels and buttons 2px, a round date stamp.
    borders: 1px folder edges. Stamps have a 3px frame with an inner ring, dashed for At risk and 4px for Behind.
    shadows: Flat offset copies of the folder in deeper manila like a stack, plus one soft drop under the main folder.
    icons:
        Inked stroke marks inside stamps, a tick for On track, a triangle
        for At risk, a cross for Behind and a clock for overdue. Steel paper
        clips are decoration.
    focus: A 3px dashed stamp blue outline offset 3px.
    tone: Office filing words in typed caps, such as Desk file, Routing slip and Received.
